== MemoryOS-inspired tiered memory ==
An agent talks through a full memory hierarchy: exchanges page out of a short queue into topic sessions, the session a retrieval keeps visiting gets hot enough to be read into a lasting profile, and the one nobody comes back to is evicted before it ever is.
Genie structures: ownership tree, three event logs, keyed collection, temporal collection, lineage DAG, versioned records, property graph

Tools available to the agent:
- add_memory: Record one exchange for alice/travel-agent. A full short-term queue (3) pages its oldest exchange into a session first, and a session over 5.0 heat is analyzed afterwards.
- retrieve_memory: Read all four tiers for a query. Every session the query reaches gets hotter.
- get_user_profile: Read the profile the analyses arrived at, and every reading it replaced.
- inspect_sessions: Read each mid-term session with its visit, length, and recency terms.
- analyze_now: Analyze the hottest session immediately, whatever its heat.
- trace_knowledge: Ask which pages one promoted fact was extracted from.
- read_dialogue_chain: Walk forward from one page along the exchanges that continued it.
- memory_stats: Read how much each tier of alice/travel-agent holds.

Agent answer:
Question: How should you book Alice's next Austin trip?
Profile on file (revision 2):
- seat_preference: window
- document_watch: passport expires March 2026
Recent exchanges still in short-term memory (3/3):
- Book the vegetarian meal for the Austin flight.
- Remind me to renew the passport in January.
- Can you start planning next month's Austin trip?
Mid-term pages retrieved for 'window seat booking passport Austin':
- [flight seat preferences] Last trip you booked a window seat and I had to have it changed. (score 0.6)
- [flight seat preferences] The window seat turned out better, so keep window from now on. (score 0.4)
- [passport and documents] My passport expires in March 2026. (score 0.2)
What is on file about the user:
- Alice switched from aisle seats to window seats. (score 0.2)
- Alice's passport expires in March 2026. (score 0.2)
What the assistant learned about doing the job:
- Confirm Alice's seat preference before booking. (score 0.4)
Why 'Alice switched from aisle seats to window seats.' is on file:
- read from: 'The window seat turned out better, so keep window from now on.'
The exchange that started the seat conversation, and what continued it:
- I always want an aisle seat when we fly.
- then: Last trip you booked a window seat and I had to have it changed.
- then: The window seat turned out better, so keep window from now on.
Where the tiers stand:
- 3/3 sessions holding 5 page(s)
- 2 user fact(s) and 1 assistant fact(s) promoted

